From bc48e4436f74f910e9faa80f489c26d9fc545348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:54:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/49] R1 (validate): compare lock-wait reads with the
 repository after confirmation

Reads started during the lock's 200 ms settle delay happen before the second
lock check. A process whose lock was confirmed before ours became visible can
change the repository and unlock inside that window; the snapshot list and
index read during the wait were then used as they were (backup deduplicated
against pruned packs and reported success).

Nothing read during the wait is used unchecked any more. After the lock is
confirmed, the snapshot files and then the index files are listed again:
- commands always work with the snapshot listing taken after confirmation;
- the index loaded during the wait is kept only if every index file it was
  built from is still listed (index files are named by the hash of their
  content); index files added in the meantime are loaded in addition, and
  only those;
- a removed snapshot or index file, or any failed read during the wait,
  discards everything read during the wait and reads it again in stock order
  (snapshots, then index). check also discards on an added index file and
  builds a new checker, because a checker's blob set is bound to the index it
  was created on.

The wait itself is untouched (internal/repository/lock_file.go is unchanged).

Also in this commit:
- a failed lock attempt leaves no prepared state behind in the command
  (repositoryIndexWaitWork and checkerIndexWaitWork clear the pointer);
- after a failed snapshot listing during the wait the index is not listed, so
  snapshots are listed before the index on that error path too;
- backup uses the same load as the other commands (backupIndexLoad is an
  alias), and no longer switches the overlap off when the debug log is on.

Outside cmd/restic, two new files and no edited one:
internal/repository/index_loaded_ids.go (Repository.LoadedIndexIDs and
Repository.LoadAddedIndexFiles; a second LoadIndex would read every index
file again) and internal/checker/snapshot_list.go
(Checker.LoadSnapshotsFromList).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
